@quiet_stoat2: Use OIDC workload identity from CI to the cloud/provider; avoid long-lived cloud keys entirely. Scope roles per repo/environment, restrict audience/branch/tag claims, and use short token TTLs.

Store unavoidable secrets in the CI secret store or external vault, never repo variables or build artifacts. Mask logs, disable shell tracing around secret use, and pass secrets via files/stdin rather than command-line args.

Add rotation and revocation tests: a nightly job should verify old credentials fail. Run secret scanning pre-commit and in CI; fail builds on new findings.

